{
  "doc": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "id": "footfall-api-image-build-and-deploy",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Footfall API image: build and deploy"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "How the Footfall Go API becomes a running container on the droplet, and the one-command path for building and deploying it repeatably."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Status: actionable runbook. The container topology decision is recorded in "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "../wiki/wp-umami-stats-plugin.md",
            "rel": "doc",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "the plan's deployment section"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " (footfall-x0i)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "the-split",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "The split"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "The split is firm: "
          },
          {
            "kind": "strong",
            "text": "this repo builds the image; ansible deploys it."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " The build half (source -\u003e image -\u003e tarball) lives here; the deploy half (tarball -\u003e running container on the VPS) is the "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#the-ansible-stats_api-role",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "ansible "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "stats_api"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " role"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " (footfall-uvc)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "what-docker-is-doing-here",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "What Docker is doing here"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "The API compiles to a single static binary with no runtime dependencies, so Docker is not here to supply a dependency environment. It does three jobs:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "items": [
          {
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "text": "Packaging"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " - wraps the binary in an immutable, content-addressed image: one versioned artifact that is byte-identical wherever it runs, so the droplet runs exactly what was built."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "text": "Hermetic build"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " - the multi-stage "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "api/Dockerfile"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " pins the toolchain ("
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "golang:1.26-alpine"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "), so the binary compiles the same way regardless of the host's Go version, or its absence (Carl has no local Go - Docker supplies it)."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "text": "Deployment unit"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " - the image is what the droplet's "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "docker compose"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " runs, on the internal proxy network with config and secrets injected by ansible. An update is \"load a new image, recreate the container\" - atomic and reversible."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "the-pipeline-end-to-end",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "The pipeline, end to end"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "diagram",
        "text": "api/ source ──▶ [build stage]      cross-compile static linux/amd64 binary\n                                   (native on the builder's arch, no emulation)\n            ──▶ [final stage]      copy binary onto distroless/static:nonroot ──▶ image\n            ──▶ docker save        image ──▶ footfall-\u003csha\u003e.tar.gz   (the artifact)\n            ──▶ transfer           tarball ──▶ VPS                    ┐\n            ──▶ docker load        tarball ──▶ image on the VPS       │ ansible\n            ──▶ docker compose up  image ──▶ running container        │ (footfall-uvc)\n            ──▶ Uptime Kuma        GET /v1/health  (runtime gate)     ┘"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Source in, image artifact out, running container on the droplet. Everything left of "
          },
          {
            "kind": "code",
            "text": "transfer"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " is this repo; everything from "
          },
          {
            "kind": "code",
            "text": "transfer"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " rightward is "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#the-ansible-stats_api-role",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "ansible"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "build-host-carl-not-the-mac",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Build host: Carl, not the Mac"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "The image is built on "
          },
          {
            "kind": "strong",
            "text": "Carl"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " (the Debian build VM where Docker lives), keeping the heavy build tooling off the Mac; the deploy is orchestrated from the Mac, which SSHes into Carl. Delivery is "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#registry-free-delivery",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "registry-free"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": ". Carl is arm64 and the droplet is amd64, which is fine and needs no second VM - see "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#cross-compiling-amd64-on-arm64-carl",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "cross-compiling amd64 on arm64"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "building",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Building"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Local build (wherever Docker runs, for inspection):"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "lang": "zsh",
        "text": "make image          # builds api/Dockerfile -\u003e footfall:\u003cgit-sha\u003e + footfall:latest"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Repeatable remote build on Carl, orchestrated from the Mac:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "lang": "zsh",
        "text": "make image-remote            # builds main on Carl, saves footfall-\u003csha\u003e.tar.gz\nmake image-remote REF=\u003cref\u003e  # build a specific branch/tag/commit instead"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "code",
            "text": "make image-remote"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " runs "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#build-image-on-carlsh",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "build-image-on-carl.sh"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": ", which SSHes into Carl, "
          },
          {
            "kind": "strong",
            "text": "refuses to build a dirty checkout"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": ", syncs it, runs "
          },
          {
            "kind": "code",
            "text": "make image"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": ", and saves "
          },
          {
            "kind": "code",
            "text": "footfall-\u003csha\u003e.tar.gz"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " beside the checkout - the artifact the "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#the-ansible-stats_api-role",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "ansible role"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " loads on the VPS."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "deploying",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Deploying"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Deploy is ansible's job (footfall-uvc), not this repo's - the "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#the-ansible-stats_api-role",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "ansible "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "stats_api"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " role"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " carries it. The footfall half is the "
          },
          {
            "kind": "code",
            "text": "make deploy"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " wrapper ("
          },
          {
            "kind": "code",
            "text": "scripts/deploy.sh"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "), which runs from the Mac only:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "lang": "zsh",
        "text": "make deploy                              # build on Carl, deploy to the default remote host\nFOOTFALL_DEPLOY_LIMIT=\u003chost\u003e make deploy # a specific inventory host\nFOOTFALL_DEPLOY_CHECK=1 make deploy      # --check dry-run (skips the build)"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Three things it guarantees:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "items": [
          {
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "text": "Remote-only guard."
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " It refuses "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "localhost"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "127.0.0.1"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "::1"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", and any "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": ".test"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " host before doing anything, so a deploy can never target the local WP test site. The default target is the "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "f5w-services"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " prod host."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "text": "Role-presence preflight."
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " If "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "roles/stats_api"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " is absent in the ansible repo it fails fast with a pointer to the queued ansible prompt - so until the role lands, "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "make deploy"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " errors clearly rather than half-deploying. This is why footfall-uvc stays open until both halves merge."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "text": "Image handoff (footfall_image_ref)."
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " It builds "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "footfall-\u003csha\u003e.tar.gz"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " on Carl, reads the build's "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_BUILD_SHA"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " marker, and passes "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "-e footfall_image_ref=\u003csha\u003e"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " to the playbook. The role reads that variable to fetch the exact matching tarball from Carl - the single, explicit contract between the two halves (documented in "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "ansible/PROMPTS.md"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ")."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#deploy-knobs-and-secrets",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Knobs and secrets"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " are env vars defined once in the script; a real deploy needs 1Password ready. Deploying today is a "
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "href": "#restart-in-place-not-blue-green",
            "rel": "detail",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "restart-in-place, not blue-green"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": ": a brief outage window each deploy, tracked as footfall-ryk."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "gotcha",
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Gotcha"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "tone": "warn",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "The Mac cannot build while "
              },
              {
                "kind": "link",
                "href": "#little-snitch-blocks-colima",
                "rel": "detail",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "Little Snitch blocks colima"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ". Since the chosen build host is Carl, this only matters if you deliberately build on the Mac."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
