      {
        "id": "build-image-on-carlsh",
        "title": "build-image-on-carl.sh",
        "source": "scripts/build-image-on-carl.sh",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "SSHes into Carl, refuses to build a dirty checkout, syncs it ("
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "git pull"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " + "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "bd dolt pull"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "), runs "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "make image"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", and "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "docker save"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "s the result to "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "footfall-\u003csha\u003e.tar.gz"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " in a directory beside the checkout. Config is overridable via "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_BUILD_HOST"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_BUILD_REPO"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_ARTIFACT_DIR"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "deploy-knobs-and-secrets",
        "title": "Deploy knobs and secrets",
        "source": "scripts/deploy.sh",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Knobs are env vars defined once in the script ("
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_DEPLOY_LIMIT"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_DEPLOY_TAG"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_DEPLOY_PLAYBOOK"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_ANSIBLE_DIR"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "FOOTFALL_DEPLOY_CHECK"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "); the playbook runs from the ansible repo so its "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "ansible.cfg"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "roles_path"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", and inventory resolve normally."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Secrets: the playbook runs under "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "op run --env-file=.op-env"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " (the ansible repo's convention), so 1Password resolves the "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "op://"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " config the role's group_vars reference - notably the view-only Umami password. "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "make deploy"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " therefore needs the "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "op"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " CLI and the ansible repo's "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": ".op-env"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", both checked in preflight. This is also why a real deploy (like any ansible run here) needs 1Password ready."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "restart-in-place-not-blue-green",
        "title": "Restart-in-place, not blue-green",
        "source": "footfall-ryk",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "As designed today, deploying is a container restart-in-place ("
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "docker compose\nup"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "/"
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "restart"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", the same pattern the "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "umami"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " role already uses), which has a brief outage window each deploy and no automatic fallback if the new image fails to come up healthy. A health-gated blue-green cutover - start the new container alongside the old one, poll "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "GET /v1/health"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", then atomically swap the Caddy-facing network alias before removing the old container - is tracked separately as footfall-ryk, depends on the ansible "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "stats_api"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " role existing, and is not yet built into this runbook's deploy plan."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "little-snitch-blocks-colima",
        "title": "Little Snitch blocks colima",
        "source": "Mac-only gotcha",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "spans": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "macOS has no Linux kernel, so the Mac's Docker runs inside a "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "text": "colima"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " Linux VM (Lima + Apple's Virtualization.framework) hosting the daemon; the "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "docker"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " CLI talks to it over a socket. When a build pulls base images, the daemon inside the VM reaches registries ("
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "docker.io"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "gcr.io"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ") through a networking helper that egresses via the Mac's stack. "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "text": "Little Snitch"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", a per-process firewall, blocks that helper, and the build fails with "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "connection refused"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " from inside the VM - not a colima bug, a firewall rule. To build on the Mac, allow the colima/Lima networking process in Little Snitch (check its log for the denied connection to "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "registry-1.docker.io"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "/"
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "gcr.io"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ")."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "findings": null
